`/ErrorBoundary.tsx` created. Usage:

```tsx
// Default fallback
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary
  fallback={(error, reset) => (
    <div>
      <p>{error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={reset}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  )}
  onError={(error, info) => reportToSentry(error, info)}
>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key details: `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error into state; `componentDidCatch` logs it and calls the optional `onError` hook; `reset` clears state to re-mount children. Custom `fallback` prop overrides the default UI entirely.
